[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: The real implementation suite has not verified several public specification postconditions, so statement coverage of the implementation unit remains incomplete: the critical-path postcondition must be exercised for a graph containing no nodes (empty path with zero cumulative weight); the scheduler state-mapping postcondition must be exercised after a node already exposed through scheduling queries is removed, confirming only currently registered nodes are reported; the skip-downstream and continue-on-error failure postconditions must be exercised across converging dependency paths so every transitive dependent becomes SKIPPED; the success postcondition must be exercised where a dependent is already terminal when another upstream succeeds, confirming terminal dependents are left unchanged while newly unblocked dependents become READY; the finished-detection postcondition must be exercised for the case where no ready nodes remain and unexecuted nodes are blocked by failed dependencies (returning True), including evaluation through upstream states that are neither SUCCEEDED nor blocking; and the runner postcondition must be exercised for FAIL_FAST when a node action fails, confirming subsequent wave execution halts and remaining pending nodes are CANCELLED in the run report.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: Remove non-contract non-empty graph precondition from compute_critical_path so the empty-DAG postcondition (empty path, zero weight) is modelable and reachable during real SUT fuzzing; fake still returns ([], 0.0) and asserts path membership/weight type.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Add real-suite scenarios addressing coverage feedback: empty-graph critical path (empty path/zero weight); scheduler state mapping after removing a node already exposed via scheduler queries (only registered nodes reported); skip-downstream and continue-on-error over converging diamond paths with independent continuation; success promotion leaving already-terminal dependents unchanged while newly unblocked dependents become READY; finished detection when an unsynced dependent is added behind a failed dependency plus a RUNNING upstream that is neither SUCCEEDED nor blocking; and FAIL_FAST runner halting after a mid-wave failure with remaining pending nodes cancelled in the report.
