[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: The real implementation suite still leaves the finished-detection contract partially unverified for in-flight execution: it never evaluates whether the DAG run is finished while a non-terminal node is still running and downstream dependents remain unexecuted, so the transitive upstream evaluation that distinguishes merely unfinished, non-succeeded ancestors from genuinely blocked ones is not exercised beyond the immediate dependency, and a shared upstream ancestor reached through converging dependency paths is never revisited. The specification requires finished-detection to report completion only when every node is terminal or when no ready nodes remain and unexecuted nodes are blocked by failed dependencies; scenario coverage of that invariant during an in-progress run, including chains whose intermediate upstream states are non-terminal and not yet blocking, and converging upstream paths, is needed to close the remaining coverage deficit.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Add in-flight finished-detection scenarios closing the transitive-upstream coverage gap: (1) a RUNNING root with a deep chain and converging left/right dependents so is_finished evaluates non-succeeded, non-blocking ancestors transitively through converging paths; (2) a failed ancestor x added-after-failure with converging y1/y2 branches feeding z and deep, so transitively blocked unexecuted nodes are detected and no ready wave remains. Both drive is_finished/next_wave/get_state/get_all_states during an in-progress run.
